Workflow Reminders:
● No commits without being explicitly asked
● No co-author attribution ever added to commits
● Follow the Handbook’s structural specifics (exact package names, file structure) rather
than improvising alternatives, unless something in the Handbook is genuinely wrong
● No code snippets belong in any of the three planning docs — if a new session starts
adding code to Proposal/Build Plan/Handbook, that’s drifting from the established
documentation style
● Test scenarios for Phase 3 risk flags should use deliberately constructed test profiles, not
real users’ profiles (Handbook Step 3.6)